---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy and data collection disclosures for CheckYourCalendar.">
  <Header />

  <main class="container main-content">
    <article class="editorial-article">
      <header class="article-header">
        <h1 class="article-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="article-subtitle">Information practices, analytics, and cookie usage disclosures</p>
      </header>

      <section class="article-body">
        <p class="lead">
          CheckYourCalendar provides multi-calendar conversions, cultural observances, and date exploration. This policy explains what information is collected when you visit our website, how analytics work, and how we handle direct communications.
        </p>

        <h2>Website Architecture & Data Storage</h2>
        <p>
          CheckYourCalendar operates as a static website. We do not offer user accounts, user logins, or profiles, and we do not maintain a database for website visitors. The site does not contain a web-based contact form that stores submissions in a database.
        </p>

        <h2>Website Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use two analytics systems to measure traffic, monitor site performance, and understand how visitors interact with our content:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics:</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to measure overall traffic volume and site performance. According to Cloudflare's documentation, Cloudflare Web Analytics is privacy-focused, does not use cookies or client-side storage for measurement, and does not collect visitors' personal data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Analytics 4:</strong> We use Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to understand site usage patterns, such as page visits, sessions, approximate geographic region (country or city level), and browser or device characteristics. The standard GA4 web implementation uses first-party analytics cookies and client identifiers (such as <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</code>) to measure interactions across browsing sessions.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cookies & Identifiers</h2>
        <p>
          Our core calendar calculations and date conversions run directly in your browser without requiring cookies. Cloudflare Web Analytics measurement also does not use cookies or client-side state. However, Google Analytics sets first-party analytics cookies on your device to collect aggregate usage statistics. You can manage or disable cookies through your browser settings, or use browser add-ons designed to opt out of Google Analytics tracking.
        </p>

        <h2>Email Correspondence</h2>
        <p>
          The website does not operate an account system or database for contact submissions. Messages sent by email are handled through our email service. If you contact us by email, we may use the information you provide to respond to your message, investigate reported calendar issues, or consider suggestions.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          Because CheckYourCalendar operates statically on Cloudflare's global content delivery network without user accounts or web databases, there is no storage of user credentials or personal profile data on our servers.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy Inquiries</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions or feedback regarding this Privacy Policy or our information practices, please contact us at:
          <br />
          <a href="mailto:inquiries@checkyourcalendar.com"><strong>inquiries@checkyourcalendar.com</strong></a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .main-content {
    padding-top: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .editorial-article {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .article-header {
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-primary);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .article-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .article-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-on-surface-variant);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .article-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-on-background);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .article-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }

  .article-body p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-on-background);
  }

  .article-body ul {
    list-style-type: square;
    padding-left: var(--spacing-lg);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-on-background);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-sm);
  }

  .article-body li {
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .article-body a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .article-body a:hover {
    color: var(--color-primary-container);
  }

  .article-body code {
    background-color: var(--color-surface-dim);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
</style>
